        "comments": "The assembly daCarCris1.hap1.1 is based on 50x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Heterozygous inversions were observed in the following regions: chromosome 5, 73.9 Mb to 80.2 Mb; chromosome 6, 26.7 Mb to 42 Mb; chromosome 8, 69.5 Mb to 70.5 Mb.",
